    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.jump\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nHello, i currently have set ignorecase & set smartcase on my vimrc.\r\nI'm enjoying the mini.jump module, but i'd prefer to keep my smartcase on / searches but not on my f/F searches.\r\nThe reasons are simple, for starters I'm already used to it functioning that way. But also, current functionality may break some custom mappings, functions or macros in my opinion.\r\nSo is it possible to configure it against my vimrc?",
